course: dictionary
lesson: 143
title: Summer sleep: aestivation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some animals have a long, deep rest to get through a hot, dry time. This rest is called aestivation. «Some animals sleep through summer instead.» Aestivation is that summer sleep.
explain: Hibernation is a winter sleep that some animals take to get through the cold. Aestivation is the summer version. The idea is the same, but the season is different: hibernation happens in the cold, and aestivation happens in the heat.
explain: Context gives you clues. «The African lungfish digs into drying mud, wraps itself in slime and waits for the rain, and that is called aestivation.» Drying mud, slime and waiting for rain all point to a long rest in dry weather, so aestivation must mean that rest.
fact: Aestivation is a noun. The verb is aestivate, as in: some animals aestivate in the dry season.
fact: Aestivation means a long, sleep-like rest in very hot, dry weather, to save water and energy.
fact: Snails, lungfish, some frogs, tortoises and crocodiles can aestivate. They hide in mud or burrows and slow down until the rain comes.
fact: «African lungfish survive the dry season sealed in slime in dried mud, breathing air, sometimes for years; this summer sleep is aestivation.»
fact: In botany, aestivation also means the way the parts of a flower bud are folded before it opens. The US spelling is estivation.
exercise: What does aestivation mean? | A dance that frogs do before the rain | A quick swim to find food in a cold river | A long winter sleep in the snow | *A long, sleep-like rest in hot, dry weather, to save water and energy
exercise: In «The African lungfish digs into drying mud and waits for the rain», which animal is aestivating? | A fox | *The African lungfish | The rain | The mud
exercise: What is the difference between hibernation and aestivation? | Aestivation is how flowers open in spring | *Hibernation is a winter sleep, and aestivation is a summer sleep | They are two different words for the same thing in the same season | Hibernation is a summer sleep and aestivation is a winter sleep
test: Which season is aestivation linked to? | Autumn | Winter | Spring | *Summer
test: Which word is the verb (the action word) for the summer sleep? | Summer | *Aestivate | Aestivation
exam: A snail hides in a burrow in a hot, dry field and sleeps until the rain returns. What is this called? | Hibernation | Migration | *Aestivation | Camouflage
